      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am still fairly new to this codebase, so I maybe mistaken but I have tried to summarize my understanding so far below\n\n\nI grepped for soong_build (a bootstrap_go_binary) in .bootstrap/build.ninja, and the definition looks something like\n```\nbuild ${g.bootstrap.buildDir}/.bootstrap/soong_build/obj/soong_build.a: $\n        g.bootstrap.compile ${g.bootstrap.srcDir}/build/soong/cmd/soong_build/main.go $\n        ${g.bootstrap.srcDir}/build/soong/cmd/soong_build/writedocs.go $\n        ${g.bootstrap.srcDir}/build/soong/cmd/soong_build/queryview.go $\n...\n(more rows)\n```\n\nWhat happens if one adds a glob pattern to bootstrap_go_binary?\nIf we add a glob pattern, the above will look like\n```\nbuild ${g.bootstrap.buildDir}/.bootstrap/soong_build/obj/soong_build.a: $\n        g.bootstrap.compile \n${g.bootstrap.srcDir}/build/soong/cmd/soong_build/*.go $\n...\n(more rows)\n```        \nand cause a compilation error. I think if we want to support globs, we have to dynamically create a list of source files somewhere around here https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/blueprint/bootstrap/bootstrap.go;l\u003d480;drc\u003dmaster\n\n\nWhy do we then handle globs while building soong_build in the first place?\nI think globs is not used to build soong_build, but is used by soong_build itself to build soong/build.ninja (via primaryBuilderArgs)\n```\nbuild out/soong/build.ninja: g.bootstrap.build.ninja Android.bp | ${builder}\n    builder \u003d ${g.bootstrap.BinDir}/soong_build\n    extra \u003d -l out/.module_paths/Android.bp.list -globFile out/soong/.bootstrap/build-globs.ninja -o out/soong/build.ninja --available_env out/soong/soong.environment.available --used_env out/soong/soong.environment.used Android.bp\ndefault out/soong/build.ninja\n```",
